WEBVTT

00:06.715 --> 00:08.717
I wonder...

00:08.800 --> 00:12.470
why is it that life always
requires us to overcome

00:12.595 --> 00:18.268
so much grief, suffering,
and all that other crap?

00:18.393 --> 00:22.939
Can't we just have fun and not
have to deal with any of it?

00:23.023 --> 00:24.649
That's what was
going through my head

00:24.774 --> 00:27.193
when first I heard about Hapna.

00:27.277 --> 00:30.697
So, obviously, I jumped on it.

00:30.780 --> 00:34.784
Some people said that it
cured the pain of a heartbreak.

00:34.909 --> 00:38.121
I thought, "That's weird."

00:38.204 --> 00:41.458
"How can a broken heart
ever be painless?"

00:42.375 --> 00:45.378
"Isn't this too good
to be true?"

00:45.462 --> 00:47.797
"What if I'm just being duped?"

00:48.840 --> 00:51.718
Those thoughts did cross
my mind.

00:53.094 --> 00:54.763
Funny...

00:54.846 --> 00:57.474
It turns out that
we were all being duped.

02:34.529 --> 02:35.405
Whoa...

02:35.530 --> 02:37.490
There's a 100,000 Skinners?

02:37.574 --> 02:39.576
He's all over the place.

02:39.659 --> 02:41.161
Wow!

02:41.244 --> 02:42.829
Get a load of that one.
- Gross.

02:42.912 --> 02:45.206
Someone must be hacking
the surveillance systems...

02:45.290 --> 02:47.500
Are they replacing
all the faces with his?

02:47.584 --> 02:50.545
Yes... and it's
being done with precision.

02:50.628 --> 02:52.422
They've altered
the polygon masks,

02:52.505 --> 02:54.757
as well as the thermal imaging.

02:54.883 --> 02:55.925
So what are you saying?

02:56.050 --> 02:57.719
Skinner is the one
behind all this?

02:57.802 --> 02:58.970
No way...

02:59.095 --> 03:00.763
I'm only aware of
three hackers...

03:00.847 --> 03:02.557
that can pull off a task
like this...

03:02.640 --> 03:05.101
And who are they?

03:05.226 --> 03:06.728
Popcorn Wizard...

03:06.811 --> 03:08.730
Doctor 909...

03:08.813 --> 03:10.481
and Mad Screamer.

03:10.607 --> 03:13.276
Oh... that last one... is me.

03:13.401 --> 03:15.445
- What?
- Seriously?

03:15.570 --> 03:16.946
There's a strong possibility,

03:17.030 --> 03:19.741
one of the other two hackers
is helping Skinner out.

03:19.824 --> 03:23.620
- Elaina, can you find them?
- I'm on it.

03:23.745 --> 03:26.372
The surveillance cameras
are no longer an option.

03:26.456 --> 03:29.042
But this does give us one clue.

03:29.125 --> 03:30.627
If Skinner has undergone
plastic surgery

03:30.710 --> 03:32.295
to change his appearance,

03:32.420 --> 03:35.006
there would be
no need to do all of this.

03:35.131 --> 03:36.299
Which means?

03:36.382 --> 03:38.468
That he's still
somewhere out there...

03:38.593 --> 03:40.094
with the same face.

03:40.178 --> 03:41.304
Correct.

03:41.387 --> 03:42.805
For now,
I want Chris and Leland

03:42.931 --> 03:45.183
to see what they can find
at Skinner's residence.

03:45.308 --> 03:47.644
I have a lead
I can follow up on, too.

03:47.769 --> 03:50.605
What lead do you have?

03:50.688 --> 03:52.649
His name is Claude Cline.

03:52.732 --> 03:56.069
He was my mentor when I worked
at the Lab at my university.

03:56.152 --> 03:58.154
In the past,
he was involved in some

03:58.238 --> 03:59.822
research projects with Skinner.

03:59.948 --> 04:02.909
We might be able to get
some kind of clue from him.

04:02.992 --> 04:04.327
Ah, man, this sucks.

04:04.410 --> 04:06.329
Why'd I have to get paired
up with you?

04:06.412 --> 04:08.039
Not a fan of you either...

04:08.164 --> 04:10.667
Just do you job
and I'll do mine.

04:10.750 --> 04:12.001
Oh, come on.

04:24.973 --> 04:26.099
We're from Smile Clean!

04:26.182 --> 04:27.433
Yeah,
and we're here to make

04:27.517 --> 04:29.269
Mr. Skinner's home
squeaky clean!

04:29.352 --> 04:32.188
Huh? Haven't you guys
been watching the news?

04:32.313 --> 04:34.732
The owner of the house
has gone missing!

04:34.857 --> 04:37.819
Okay, but we were told
we'd be paid up-front, so...

04:37.902 --> 04:39.153
I don't care.

04:39.237 --> 04:41.739
I was told not to let
anybody get inside!

04:42.991 --> 04:44.701
All right then, sir.

04:44.826 --> 04:47.745
We'll just have them send
the invoice to the both of you.

04:47.870 --> 04:48.913
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

04:49.038 --> 04:50.498
Well, there's a cancellation fee

04:50.581 --> 04:52.792
if you send us back
without doing our job...

04:52.875 --> 04:54.210
And just between us...

04:54.335 --> 04:56.296
it's actually
a pretty hefty amount...

04:59.048 --> 05:01.009
This is on your heads!

05:01.092 --> 05:03.011
You people are the ones
who prescribed me

05:03.094 --> 05:04.387
this crap in the first place!

05:04.512 --> 05:06.389
So do something!

05:06.514 --> 05:08.516
Ah-ah-choo!

05:08.599 --> 05:10.685
Ah!

05:12.854 --> 05:14.397
Hold up.

05:14.522 --> 05:15.565
Where's your mentor?

05:15.648 --> 05:17.108
They say he retired

05:17.233 --> 05:19.736
and they don't have any
information on his whereabouts.

05:19.861 --> 05:22.530
- Oh, yeah?
- However...

05:22.613 --> 05:25.033
there's a rumor
that he ended up on the streets.

05:25.116 --> 05:28.286
If that's the case, I might be
able to help you find him.

05:28.411 --> 05:29.829
Great...

05:29.912 --> 05:32.582
Care to explain
why you're so good at this?

05:32.707 --> 05:34.167
Really? You think so?

05:34.250 --> 05:35.501
You're just playing dumb.

05:35.585 --> 05:37.420
The same could be said
about you.

05:37.545 --> 05:39.672
I'm not the one hiding
anything...

05:39.756 --> 05:41.591
Okay then,
what did you do

05:41.674 --> 05:43.426
before you ended up
on this team?

05:43.509 --> 05:46.929
I traveled all over
the world as a secret agent.

05:47.013 --> 05:48.306
Yeah, right.

05:48.431 --> 05:50.016
Let's see here...

05:54.270 --> 05:56.439
Oh, nice.
It's opened.

05:56.564 --> 05:59.150
Cleaning crew!

05:59.275 --> 06:00.777
Pardon us!

06:08.743 --> 06:12.288
There sure is a lot of them
out here.

06:12.372 --> 06:14.999
So, where's this lead of yours?

06:15.124 --> 06:16.209
Guy's name is Jerry.

06:16.292 --> 06:18.044
Met him in prison,
two stays ago.

06:18.127 --> 06:21.672
Now I hear he's the leader
of this homeless community.

06:21.798 --> 06:24.133
What? You scared or something?

06:24.217 --> 06:26.177
Absolutely not.

06:26.302 --> 06:27.887
Ugh!

06:27.970 --> 06:30.515
You don't have to act
all tough in front of me.

06:30.640 --> 06:31.808
Let's go.

06:59.544 --> 07:02.713
- I betcha he got busted.
- Are you serious?

07:02.839 --> 07:05.216
Hey, guys, do you
know anyone named Jerry?

07:05.341 --> 07:07.677
He's supposed to be
in charge of things around here.

07:07.760 --> 07:10.346
- Jerry?
- No clue.

07:10.471 --> 07:11.639
Excuse me.

07:11.722 --> 07:13.516
Do you know a man named Jerry?

07:13.641 --> 07:15.017
Hey, buddy.

07:15.143 --> 07:18.020
The guy you're talking to
can't see anything.

07:19.355 --> 07:20.815
Nothing of value
to us here, huh?

07:20.898 --> 07:21.983
Yep.

07:22.066 --> 07:22.984
And it's no surprise

07:23.067 --> 07:24.152
since the FBI and cops

07:24.235 --> 07:25.862
already swept this place.

07:25.945 --> 07:28.698
Gotta say, this house is
pretty unremarkable considering

07:28.823 --> 07:31.367
it's owned by
a super famous scientist.

07:31.492 --> 07:33.035
Know what I mean?

07:33.161 --> 07:35.288
- Hm.
- Is that Hapna?

07:35.371 --> 07:37.582
Doesn't look like it.

07:37.707 --> 07:38.875
You don't suppose...

07:38.958 --> 07:41.294
this thing could be a
cure to Hapna?

07:41.377 --> 07:42.879
You're joking, right?

07:43.004 --> 07:45.756
Yeah, there's no way.

07:45.882 --> 07:47.717
You're not one of us, are ya?

07:47.842 --> 07:50.720
Jill's the one who runs
the show around this place.

07:50.803 --> 07:52.638
- Jill?
- That's right.

07:52.722 --> 07:54.891
She's right behind you.

07:57.268 --> 07:59.687
Oh, my gosh! Axel?!

07:59.770 --> 08:02.148
- Huh...?
-  It's been forever!

08:02.231 --> 08:05.568
I'm so happy to see you!
Just look at you!

08:05.693 --> 08:07.195
You haven't changed a bit!

08:07.278 --> 08:08.863
Thanks! And look at you!

08:08.946 --> 08:10.656
You're a woman now, Jerry!

08:10.740 --> 08:12.200
Yep! I go by Jill now!

08:12.283 --> 08:14.327
Well, I'm digging
your new look, Jill!

08:14.410 --> 08:16.162
Oh, you! C'mere! Mm!

08:17.997 --> 08:20.625
Wait...

08:22.126 --> 08:24.587
Oh, my, how many
centuries has it been?

08:24.712 --> 08:26.631
I thought that you were back
in the slammer.

08:26.756 --> 08:28.257
Yeah, but then I got out again.

08:28.341 --> 08:29.592
Another prison break?

08:29.675 --> 08:32.261
- Kinda.
- You never learn.

08:32.345 --> 08:34.889
So, what brings you here?

08:34.972 --> 08:37.683
We're looking for a man
named Claude.

08:37.767 --> 08:39.727
I was told he's
been seen somewhere

08:39.810 --> 08:42.021
around this area recently.

08:43.231 --> 08:44.357
Listen.

08:44.440 --> 08:46.567
I'm a transgender woman
with a record,

08:46.651 --> 08:48.945
who's also gone
through bankruptcy.

08:49.070 --> 08:51.280
Around here,
that's not an uncommon story.

08:51.364 --> 08:53.991
Some folks were happy
to hear the world is ending...

08:54.116 --> 08:56.953
Even though you'll
never hear them say it out loud.

08:57.078 --> 09:00.122
These people have circumstances
that have led them here.

09:00.248 --> 09:02.792
So you have to understand
that it's common courtesy

09:02.875 --> 09:05.836
not to go digging up
anybody's past.

09:07.922 --> 09:08.923
Well...

09:09.006 --> 09:11.634
Back when I was an
academic researcher,

09:11.717 --> 09:12.927
a guy said to me...

09:13.010 --> 09:15.137
"There will never be
a black Einstein."

09:15.221 --> 09:18.140
And that it was impossible
for people like us

09:18.224 --> 09:19.809
to win a Nobel Prize...

09:19.892 --> 09:22.478
no matter how hard "we" tried.

09:22.603 --> 09:25.523
Unfortunately,
I ended up hitting him...

09:25.648 --> 09:29.652
That man...
was the dean of the university.

09:29.735 --> 09:32.321
I was kicked out of the
academy for my actions,

09:32.446 --> 09:37.535
but Professor Claude stood up
for me until the very end.

09:37.660 --> 09:39.787
And to this day...

09:39.870 --> 09:41.289
I have yet to thank him.

09:44.834 --> 09:46.919
Show me his picture.

09:47.003 --> 09:48.838
What's the matter, Professor?

09:48.921 --> 09:50.464
Whoop his butt already.

09:50.548 --> 09:51.632
Hm...

09:51.716 --> 09:53.009
Queen to Bishop.

09:53.092 --> 09:54.343
Huh?

09:54.468 --> 09:56.387
Hm.

09:56.512 --> 09:57.847
The Professor's gonna win.

09:57.972 --> 09:59.348
Oh, yeah, it's over.

10:00.975 --> 10:02.560
Bishop to King, checkmate.

10:02.685 --> 10:04.604
Oh.

10:05.438 --> 10:07.481
- He got it!
- No way!

10:07.565 --> 10:09.483
Now I'm out 3 days worth
of food!

10:09.567 --> 10:11.193
Goddammit!

10:11.319 --> 10:13.029
Is that you, Doug?

10:13.112 --> 10:15.031
It's been a long time...

10:15.114 --> 10:16.657
Professor.

10:16.741 --> 10:19.452
Yo, dude!

10:19.535 --> 10:21.662
Wanna play a game against me?

10:23.664 --> 10:24.915
You must be surprised.

10:25.041 --> 10:27.084
Seeing how I've hit
rock bottom like this.

10:27.209 --> 10:29.503
To be honest,
I need your help.

10:29.587 --> 10:31.547
I'm looking for Skinner
right now.

10:31.631 --> 10:33.215
Ah, yes.

10:33.299 --> 10:34.634
Things are a real mess.

10:34.717 --> 10:37.386
Do you happen to know
where he might be?

10:37.511 --> 10:38.888
Hm.

10:39.013 --> 10:42.892
I haven't talked with that
man for years.

10:43.559 --> 10:44.810
Little did I know,

10:44.894 --> 10:47.021
that humanity would
one day be killed,

10:47.104 --> 10:48.773
by the medicine he invented.

10:48.898 --> 10:51.067
Any information would help
no matter how trivial.

10:51.150 --> 10:52.902
Hm.

10:56.405 --> 10:58.491
- Professor?
- Huh?

10:58.574 --> 10:59.659
Right...

11:02.411 --> 11:04.747
It's gonna be one-on-one.

11:04.830 --> 11:06.290
You take the ball first.

11:06.415 --> 11:08.292
How's 20 bucks a game sound?

11:08.417 --> 11:10.419
Sounds good to me!

11:11.587 --> 11:13.381
I imagine
that Skinner was someone

11:13.464 --> 11:16.884
who most people saw
as an honorable man.

11:16.967 --> 11:18.427
But he was obsessed...

11:18.511 --> 11:22.098
His research blinded him
to everything around him.

11:22.181 --> 11:23.766
Including the time of day,

11:23.849 --> 11:26.227
and that made him a nuisance
to all the people

11:26.310 --> 11:28.104
he worked with...

11:28.813 --> 11:30.064
It was exhausting,

11:30.147 --> 11:32.358
and I knew I wouldn't
able to keep up...

11:33.734 --> 11:36.904
So, I just cut
all ties with him.

11:36.987 --> 11:40.324
But then as I watched him rise
to prominence,

11:40.449 --> 11:41.784
it made me jealous.

11:41.909 --> 11:44.662
I desperately wanted
to outdo him.

11:44.787 --> 11:47.748
To somehow leave my mark
on the world.

11:47.832 --> 11:49.709
And that frustration drove me

11:49.792 --> 11:52.795
to falsify the results
of my research.

11:52.920 --> 11:55.589
It lead
to the university firing me...

11:55.673 --> 11:57.258
and that's how I ended up here.

11:58.592 --> 12:00.761
Ugh!

12:06.100 --> 12:08.686
No way!
How's that fair?!

12:08.811 --> 12:10.271
Oh, right...

12:10.354 --> 12:11.564
I just remembered.

12:11.647 --> 12:12.940
This one time we got into

12:13.023 --> 12:15.401
a passionate discussion
about baklava...

12:15.484 --> 12:16.736
Baklava?

12:16.819 --> 12:19.238
Isn't that a
middle eastern pastry?

12:19.321 --> 12:20.322
Yes.

12:20.406 --> 12:21.407
Skinner told us

12:21.490 --> 12:22.783
that his Grandmother Belinda

12:22.867 --> 12:24.577
made the best baklava
in the world.

12:24.660 --> 12:27.872
He raved on about
how magical her recipe was,

12:27.997 --> 12:29.957
and that no one
could ever make it the same way.

12:30.040 --> 12:31.375
His grandmother?

12:31.500 --> 12:32.835
As I remember...

12:32.960 --> 12:35.588
he mentioned she lived
somewhere in Istanbul.

12:35.671 --> 12:39.258
But I couldn't tell you
if she's still around now.

12:40.926 --> 12:43.137
Thank you, Professor.

12:43.220 --> 12:46.974
And I appreciate you
standing up for me back then.

12:47.475 --> 12:48.559
Huh?

12:51.562 --> 12:52.813
Ugh!

12:57.693 --> 12:59.403
No freakin' way!

13:02.198 --> 13:05.367
So, tell me.
Do you guys go way back?

13:05.493 --> 13:07.787
No... We just met.

13:07.870 --> 13:09.371
Well, as you can see...

13:09.455 --> 13:12.374
Axel is the type of guy who
can easily make himself at home.

13:12.500 --> 13:15.377
Doesn't matter where he is,
even prison.

13:16.712 --> 13:18.506
But then,
before you know it,

13:18.589 --> 13:20.466
he just up and vanishes.

13:20.549 --> 13:21.801
I tell ya, that one...

13:21.884 --> 13:23.427
he's a real mystery.

13:23.552 --> 13:27.306
Just be careful who you try
to swindle next time.

13:27.389 --> 13:28.516
Damn.

13:28.599 --> 13:30.476
Don't ever come back here!

13:30.559 --> 13:31.936
Let's get outta here.

13:32.061 --> 13:33.437
You found your clue, didn't cha?

13:33.562 --> 13:35.064
Hm? Yeah.

13:35.147 --> 13:36.357
See you around, Jill!

13:36.440 --> 13:37.733
Come back soon, Axel!

13:37.817 --> 13:40.277
I'll be waiting for ya,
sweetie!

13:54.041 --> 13:55.751
No ID number.

13:55.876 --> 13:58.546
No tax records,
and no social security.

13:58.629 --> 14:01.048
There's nothing coming up
for Skinner's grandmother

14:01.131 --> 14:03.884
on any database
under the name of "Belinda."

14:03.968 --> 14:05.427
Does she really exist?

14:05.553 --> 14:08.389
I mean, even Skinner
has a grandmother...

14:08.472 --> 14:11.433
Actually,
we have no data on her.

14:11.517 --> 14:13.894
Maybe it was erased
intentionally?

14:13.978 --> 14:15.271
That's a possibility.

14:15.354 --> 14:18.023
- Guys, hold on. Check this out.
- Hm?

14:18.107 --> 14:20.568
This area is known
for its high crime rate.

14:20.651 --> 14:24.113
No surveillance cameras
or visual data available.

14:24.196 --> 14:27.366
Sounds like a perfect hideout.
Skinner might be there.

14:27.449 --> 14:29.827
I think we might
be getting lured into a trap...

14:29.952 --> 14:31.412
Can't deny that.

14:31.495 --> 14:34.123
Then we should go
and see it for ourselves, right?

14:34.206 --> 14:35.749
It takes about 6 hours...

14:35.833 --> 14:38.544
Take the Hyper Cube
to Istanbul...

14:38.627 --> 14:40.921
Sounds like our only option.

15:03.611 --> 15:04.820
We finally made it here!

15:04.904 --> 15:07.239
Leland, what are you wearing?

15:07.323 --> 15:10.117
Well, you know, I figured
it was best to blend in

15:10.200 --> 15:13.829
since they said it's
not safe around these parts.

15:13.913 --> 15:15.915
Do you think it's working?

15:15.998 --> 15:17.499
Yeah, I'm sure it is.

15:17.583 --> 15:19.960
Hey, hold up!
Where are you going?

15:20.044 --> 15:22.755
I'm gonna prance around town
for a while.

15:22.838 --> 15:25.007
That should get their attention.

15:25.132 --> 15:27.760
We're dealing with targets
who mask their traces,

15:27.843 --> 15:30.679
so I set up some float traps.

15:30.804 --> 15:32.014
And that's what these are?

15:32.097 --> 15:34.683
Yes.
They monitor all transactions

15:34.808 --> 15:35.976
that go through the node point.

15:36.060 --> 15:37.853
I performed a
pseudo-deconstruction

15:37.937 --> 15:39.605
on the multiple
compression functions

15:39.688 --> 15:40.689
of the hash algorithm.

15:40.773 --> 15:42.691
Uh, layman's terms, please.

15:42.775 --> 15:44.693
Essentially, they're decoys.

15:44.818 --> 15:47.363
That makes sense...

15:50.449 --> 15:51.200
Huh?

15:51.325 --> 15:53.285
Ugh! Oh, hello there.

15:53.369 --> 15:55.913
Let me just say that, um, we're
not here to cause any trouble!

15:56.038 --> 15:59.667
Well, Except for the fact
that we do look super sketchy.

15:59.750 --> 16:01.752
So, in times like these...

16:01.877 --> 16:02.962
we run for it!

16:03.045 --> 16:05.881
Huh?! Hey, wait! Ugh!

16:09.718 --> 16:11.470
- Ugh!
- Uh-oh.

16:18.143 --> 16:19.353
Let's go!

16:19.436 --> 16:20.896
Whoa!

16:31.073 --> 16:31.949
Aah!

16:33.909 --> 16:35.244
- Time to jump!
- Huh?!

16:38.038 --> 16:40.791
Here is your chamomile tea.

16:40.916 --> 16:42.084
Why, thank you.

16:42.167 --> 16:44.670
Do you know
where the prince is at?

16:48.424 --> 16:49.633
Aah!

16:52.761 --> 16:53.846
Hey...

16:53.929 --> 16:55.431
It's the prince!

16:55.514 --> 16:56.765
What the?

16:56.849 --> 16:59.351
Where'd you go now?

16:59.435 --> 17:01.395
Here you are, Your Highness.

17:01.478 --> 17:03.939
Oh, sorry,
but I'm kinda in a hurry...

17:04.064 --> 17:05.774
Huh?!

17:08.861 --> 17:10.696
Hey, stop it!

17:10.779 --> 17:12.573
It's not a watch!

17:12.656 --> 17:13.615
Leave it alone!

17:13.741 --> 17:15.993
Ugh!

17:16.118 --> 17:17.828
Enough already...

17:19.204 --> 17:20.956
Aah!

17:27.254 --> 17:28.964
Please, no!

17:31.175 --> 17:32.843
Listen...

17:32.968 --> 17:34.636
the only reason we came here

17:34.720 --> 17:38.140
is to eat some
of Grandma Belinda's baklava!

17:38.223 --> 17:39.349
Baklava?

17:39.475 --> 17:41.351
- Baklava?
- Belinda?

17:41.477 --> 17:42.770
- Huh?
- Belinda?

17:42.853 --> 17:44.188
Belinda...

17:44.313 --> 17:45.731
Oh...

17:45.814 --> 17:47.524
Huh?

17:48.650 --> 17:51.445
So, how's the
Istanbul team doing?

17:51.528 --> 17:53.614
I haven't heard anything.

17:53.697 --> 17:55.365
Maybe they're dead?

17:55.491 --> 17:57.493
According to their vitals
on their bracelets,

17:57.576 --> 17:59.244
we at least know they're alive.

17:59.328 --> 18:00.746
Well, okay then.

18:00.829 --> 18:02.164
But frankly,

18:02.247 --> 18:04.249
I don't understand
why Hersch made Leland go.

18:04.333 --> 18:06.835
Aren't we better suited
for this mission?

18:06.960 --> 18:08.837
Hm...

18:08.921 --> 18:11.840
He gives off grandson vibes.

18:13.634 --> 18:15.219
Coming!

18:15.344 --> 18:18.806
Yes, I know.
Just hold on a moment!

18:18.889 --> 18:20.474
Thanks for waiting.

18:20.557 --> 18:24.478
Are you boys the visitors who
came from out of town to see me?

18:24.561 --> 18:25.729
Uh, yes ma'am!

18:25.854 --> 18:28.190
This is for you lads.

18:28.315 --> 18:31.151
Yes!

18:31.235 --> 18:33.112
Well, don't just stand there.

18:33.195 --> 18:34.822
Come on in!

18:34.905 --> 18:36.323
I'm sorry, Miss Belinda.

18:36.406 --> 18:37.699
We hate to drop in on you
unannounced like this...

18:37.783 --> 18:40.536
Those boys
didn't mean any harm.

18:40.661 --> 18:42.830
They're just misguided.
- Really?

18:42.913 --> 18:44.706
I hope
you can forgive them.

18:44.790 --> 18:46.125
No worries...

18:46.208 --> 18:48.669
I'm sorry I had to roughed
them up a little bit.

18:48.752 --> 18:52.256
Well, here's the baklava
you've been craving.

18:52.381 --> 18:53.799
- Ooh!
- Ooh!

18:53.882 --> 18:55.217
Eat as much as you'd like.

18:55.342 --> 18:56.927
So sweet!

18:57.052 --> 18:59.096
And tasty!

18:59.221 --> 19:01.265
Awesome!

19:01.390 --> 19:03.725
Pace yourselves, boys.

19:05.269 --> 19:08.105
Would you mind
telling me who you two are?

19:08.230 --> 19:09.940
Please don't share this
with anyone,

19:10.065 --> 19:11.150
but the truth is...

19:13.026 --> 19:14.653
we're secret agents.

19:14.736 --> 19:16.071
- Huh?
- Huh?

19:16.155 --> 19:17.281
Do you mean...

19:17.406 --> 19:18.949
like James Bond?

19:19.074 --> 19:20.659
- Yeah... Something like that...
- Ooh!

19:20.742 --> 19:23.620
- No! You can't say that!
- It's all right...

19:23.745 --> 19:25.831
We're all about transparency
these days.

19:25.914 --> 19:29.626
So... do you have
a "License to Kill"?

19:29.751 --> 19:32.421
Of course.

19:34.339 --> 19:35.757
Very well, then...

19:35.841 --> 19:39.219
You must be here
to ask about my grandson.

19:39.303 --> 19:41.805
It's been years
since I last saw him.

19:41.930 --> 19:45.100
It's not like
I was keeping it a secret.

19:45.225 --> 19:48.854
It's just that no one
ever bothered to ask me.

19:49.855 --> 19:51.857
Still nothing?

19:51.940 --> 19:53.901
No...

19:53.984 --> 19:56.778
They say patience is a virtue.

19:56.904 --> 20:00.908
You see, he tragically lost
both of his parents

20:00.991 --> 20:02.409
when he was little.

20:02.492 --> 20:05.996
So I stepped up to raise him
in his mother's absence.

20:06.121 --> 20:07.497
What was he like?

20:07.623 --> 20:09.583
He was a normal little boy,

20:09.666 --> 20:12.294
and a kindhearted crybaby.

20:12.377 --> 20:15.130
Nothing unusual there.

20:15.255 --> 20:17.049
No matter the years...

20:17.132 --> 20:19.009
or the chaos he has caused...

20:19.134 --> 20:24.556
To me... he's still just the
cute little grandson I raised.

20:27.684 --> 20:28.852
That's weird.

20:28.977 --> 20:31.146
I think I've seen
this flower somewhere before.

20:31.230 --> 20:32.564
Ah, that's right...

20:32.648 --> 20:34.816
That is something
he brought for me.

20:34.942 --> 20:38.320
Apparently, it's a very rare
variety of tulip

20:38.403 --> 20:39.780
that hardly blooms.

20:39.863 --> 20:42.199
Do you remember the last time
you talked to Skinner?

20:42.324 --> 20:45.744
Let's see...
about 3 years back.

20:45.827 --> 20:47.287
Yes. That's right.

20:47.371 --> 20:49.748
He sent me a video message.

20:49.831 --> 20:51.166
Wait here a moment.

20:51.291 --> 20:54.169
They're not moving...

20:54.253 --> 20:56.171
Not an inch...

20:56.255 --> 20:59.174
What are they wasting time on?

20:59.258 --> 21:00.842
<i>Hello, Belinda!</i>

21:00.926 --> 21:02.344
<i>How have you been?</i>

21:02.427 --> 21:04.721
<i>I've been pretty busy
with work lately.</i>

21:04.846 --> 21:07.474
<i>I wanted to visit for Christmas
and have your baklava,</i>

21:07.557 --> 21:10.519
<i>but it seems like I'm not
going to be able to make it.</i>

21:10.602 --> 21:13.438
<i>Once things settle down,
I promise I'll come home.</i>

21:13.522 --> 21:16.066
<i>So take good care of yourself
until then.</i>

21:16.191 --> 21:18.277
<i>Bye for now.</i>

21:21.113 --> 21:23.865
I gotta say, that doesn't
look like the kind of guy

21:23.949 --> 21:27.369
who would commit the world's
worst massacre.

21:27.494 --> 21:31.623
A fresh batch of my baklava
is almost ready, boys!

21:31.707 --> 21:33.709
Great!

21:33.834 --> 21:36.003
- Hm. It's Skinner.
- Huh?

21:36.086 --> 21:38.714
He's gotta be watching us
from somewhere.

21:38.797 --> 21:41.967
He wants to make sure
that Belinda is okay.

21:43.218 --> 21:44.511
So do you think...

21:44.594 --> 21:46.346
he's watching us right now?

21:54.813 --> 21:56.898
What is that?

21:56.982 --> 21:58.275
<i>Yo, Skinner.</i>

21:58.400 --> 21:59.568
<i>You see me in there?!</i>

21:59.693 --> 22:01.069
<i>Remember this face!</i>

22:01.194 --> 22:02.279
<i>I'm coming after you!</i>

22:02.404 --> 22:04.323
<i>Your ass is mine!</i>

22:09.161 --> 22:10.037
They took the bait!

22:10.120 --> 22:11.580
Who? Where?

22:11.663 --> 22:15.042
I've figured out where
Doctor 909's hidden wallet is!

22:15.125 --> 22:16.418
Hidden wallet?

22:16.501 --> 22:19.546
Time to get wrecked.

22:44.988 --> 22:47.282
♪ I ♪

22:47.407 --> 22:52.496
♪ I must be
losing my mind ♪

22:52.621 --> 22:57.417
♪ I keep on trying
to find a way out ♪

22:57.501 --> 22:58.960
♪ There's no need ♪

22:59.086 --> 23:04.257
♪ You don't lock
the door anymore ♪

23:08.011 --> 23:09.179
♪ I ♪

23:09.304 --> 23:10.806
♪ Ba, ba, ba, ba ♪

23:10.889 --> 23:14.017
♪ You know I
never go out ♪

23:14.142 --> 23:15.685
♪ Ba, ba, ba, ba ♪

23:15.811 --> 23:20.482
♪ And you know I
start to forget things ♪

23:20.565 --> 23:28.490
♪ It's okay they weren't
essential anyway ♪
